  {
    "Question_Number": 77,
    "Question_Text": "In a derangement problem: There are four school sections A, B, C, D and their class teachers P, Q, R, S. A unit test is conducted, and a class teacher cannot invigilate their own section. How many such combinations of invigilators are possible?",
    "Option_A": "9",
    "Option_B": "12",
    "Option_C": "18",
    "Option_D": "24",
    "Correct_Answer": "Option A",
    "Brief_Explanation": "This is a classical derangement of 4 elements. Formula: D_4 = 4! * (1/2! - 1/3! + 1/4!) = 24 * (1/2 - 1/6 + 1/24) = 24 * (9/24) = 9 combinations."
  },
