    "Question_Number": 89,
    "Question_Text": "In a Normal Distribution Curve, what is the value of standard scores (Z-score) at the arithmetic mean of the distribution?",
    "Option_A": "0",
    "Option_B": "1",
    "Option_C": "1.96",
    "Option_D": "2.58",
    "Correct_Answer": "Option A",
    "Brief_Explanation": "Z-score is defined as (X - Mean) / SD. At the mean, X = Mean, so the Z-score is exactly zero."
  },
